Change is hard. When you want to make a change in your life, whether it's eating healthier food, starting an exercise program or saving more money, there are many human foibles that can stand in your way. Impulsivity, laziness, procrastination, or just plain forgetfulness are among them. Libraries are full of books offering multi-step plans and other tactics to inspire a new you. Often though, these plans fall flat. Our best intentions aren't enough to overcome the roadblocks of human nature that stand in our way. But in recent years, psychologists have begun to look at behavior change from a different angle. Instead of fighting human nature, this research suggests that we should analyze it and then leverage it to work for us rather than against us.
改变是艰难的。当你想要改变生活中的某样东西，不管是吃得更健康、开始锻炼计划还是存更多的钱，都有许多人类的缺点会阻碍你。冲动、懒惰、拖延或纯粹的健忘都在其中。图书馆里摆满了各种书籍，提供多步骤的计划和其他策略来激发一个全新的你。然而，这些计划往往收效甚微。我们最好的意愿不足以克服阻碍我们前进的人性路障。但在近年来，心理学家开始从不同的角度来看待行为改变。这项研究表明，我们不应该与人性对抗，而应该分析它，然后加以利用，让它为我们服务，而不是与我们作对。

